{
  "uid": "morph-overview",
  "title": "Desire Path — is it up, fast, correct, and learning?",
  "description": "The four questions in the order an incident asks them. Every panel carries its own description; hover it rather than guessing what the number means.",
  "tags": ["morph", "overview"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": false,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {
    "refresh_intervals": ["10s", "30s", "1m", "5m", "15m"]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is it up?",
      "description": "The first question during an incident, and the only one worth asking before the others. Everything below this row assumes the answer is yes.",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Services answering",
      "description": "How many of the three scrape targets are responding. Two out of three is an outage even when the site still loads: the worker being down means the site has quietly stopped adapting, which looks completely normal from a browser.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 2
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "count(up{job=~\"morph-.*\"} == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 2
              },
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Ingest error rate",
      "description": "Share of beacons the collector could not accept, over five minutes. The IngestErrorRate alert fires above 1%. A rate that is exactly zero for hours and then jumps is usually the broker, not the collector.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 5,
        "y": 2
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(morph_ingest_errors_total[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(morph_ingest_requests_total[5m])), 0.001)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 0.005
              },
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": 0.01
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "What is the queue backlog doing?",
      "description": "Waiting jobs per queue. A backlog that rises and falls is a busy worker; one that rises monotonically is a dead consumer, and the difference is the shape rather than the height. QueueBacklog alerts above 10,000.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 14,
        "x": 10,
        "y": 2
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "morph_queue_waiting",
          "legendFormat": "{{queue}} waiting",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "morph_queue_failed",
          "legendFormat": "{{queue}} failed",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is it fast?",
      "description": "The three budgets §7 sets, each on its own panel with its own threshold, so a breach is a colour rather than an axis to read.",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Is ingest inside its 25 ms budget?",
      "description": "p99 of the collector, which is the number §7 budgets at 25 ms and the one bench/ingest.js gates on. p50 is drawn alongside because the gap between them is the useful signal: a p99 climbing while p50 holds is queueing, not slowness.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(morph_ingest_lag_ms_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p99 ingest lag",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum(rate(morph_ingest_lag_ms_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p50 ingest lag",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 3000
              },
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": 5000
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Is the adaptive decision inside its 5 ms budget?",
      "description": "p95 and p99 of resolving a full eleven-surface assignment. This excludes the snapshot read on purpose: §7 budgets the decision, and folding a cache miss into it would make the budget look breached by a network round trip the decision does not perform. DecisionLatency alerts on p95 above 5 ms.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(morph_decision_duration_ms_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 decision",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(morph_decision_duration_ms_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p99 decision",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 3
              },
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": 5
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Are the Core Web Vitals inside budget?",
      "description": "p75 of each vital, which is the percentile the budgets are written against and the one the rollback guardrail quarantines on. The same numbers Lighthouse enforces in CI, so a variant cannot pass the gate and then be removed in production for the number the gate approved.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "morph_web_vital_p75",
          "legendFormat": "{{metric}} p75",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Is any process leaking?",
      "description": "Resident set per service. Read across hours rather than minutes: a leak of a megabyte an hour is invisible in any single sample and unmistakable across a shift, and it is the failure bench/soak.js exists to find.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 18
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "process_resident_memory_bytes",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is it correct?",
      "description": "A site can be up and fast while adapting on conclusions from last Tuesday. These are the panels that catch that, and none of them is visible from a browser.",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "How stale is the decision set?",
      "description": "Age of the posterior snapshot the renderer is actually serving — measured at the renderer, not at the worker that wrote it, because the disagreement between those two is exactly what is worth being able to see. The adapt job runs hourly, so anything past two hours means it has stopped.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "max(morph_snapshot_age_seconds)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 7200
              },
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": 14400
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "How far behind is the adaptive loop?",
      "description": "Seconds between now and the last hour folded into the posteriors. This is the one number that says whether the site is still learning at all; every other panel in this row can look healthy while it climbs.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 28
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "time() - max(morph_adapt_cycle_hour_seconds)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 7200
              },
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": 14400
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Are events arriving, and at what rate?",
      "description": "Events accepted per second, not requests: a beacon carries between one and fifty, so the two curves diverge whenever batching changes. A flat line at zero with services up means the collector is answering and nothing is sending.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 28
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(morph_ingest_events_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "events/s",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(morph_ingest_requests_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "beacons/s",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is it learning?",
      "description": "The row that distinguishes this system from a website. Everything above can be green while the bandit has quietly stopped exploring and frozen on a variant that stopped working weeks ago.",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 35
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Is the adaptation actually beating the baseline?",
      "description": "Measured lift of the adaptive cohort over the pinned 5% holdout. This is the whole product in one number, and it is the only honest one: it compares the system against itself rather than against a guess. Negative means the adaptation is doing harm and NegativeHoldoutLift fires.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "morph_holdout_lift_relative",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Is it still exploring?",
      "description": "Share of impressions going to something other than the leader. A bandit that has stopped exploring still serves pages and still reports a healthy reward — it has simply lost the ability to notice the world changed, and it looks like success until the day the best variant is no longer the best. ExplorationCollapsed fires below 0.5%.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 36
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "morph_exploration_rate",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "max": 1,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 0.005
              },
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": 0.02
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "What is the engine removing, and why?",
      "description": "Retirements come from the reward statistics; quarantines come from the health guardrail on Core Web Vitals, client errors and bounce rate. They are separate series because they mean different things: a burst of quarantines is a deploy that broke something, a steady trickle of retirements is the system working as designed.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 36
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
